' processing/launcher.py; processing/launcher_models.py; processing/launcher_aws.py
title DP-1 solution: durable capacity roles
top to bottom direction
class "launcher" as l <<module / capacity gate>> $PROC {
 _reserve(factory, config, obs, visible, *, launching)
 _send(factory, ecs, token, config=None)
 observe(ecs, config, known_arns=())
}
class LauncherControl <<serialization root>> $PROC {
 id: int = 1
 enabled: bool
 enabled_at: datetime | None
}
class LaunchReservation <<durable reservation>> $PROC {
 token: str
 started_by: str
 payload: dict
 status: str
 deadline_at: datetime
 task_arn: str | None
}
class EcsPort <<adapter>> $INFRA {
 run_task(payload)
 list_tasks(desired_status)
 describe_tasks(arns)
}
l --> LauncherControl : exclusive reserve / shared send
l --> LaunchReservation : commit before start
LauncherControl "1" -- "0..*" LaunchReservation : logical association
l ..> EcsPort : stable token + payload
note bottom of LaunchReservation
 Pattern roles annotate actual types.
 Independent of Job/Attempt ownership.
 No association FK; selected signatures
 omit implicit self.
end note
@enduml
